1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,034
Add the odd numbers in order, each in its own color, and watch what

2
00:00:04,134 --> 00:00:07,776
the sums make. One. One plus three is four.

3
00:00:07,876 --> 00:00:12,578
One plus three plus five is nine. Add seven: sixteen. Add nine:

4
00:00:12,678 --> 00:00:13,404
twenty-five.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,546
Look at the answers. One is one times one. Four is two times two.

6
00:00:18,646 --> 00:00:22,531
Nine is three times three. Sixteen is four times four.

7
00:00:22,631 --> 00:00:26,772
Twenty-five is five times five. Every sum is a square number.

8
00:00:26,872 --> 00:00:28,330
Yellow marks what to look at.

9
00:00:28,416 --> 00:00:30,736
Now count the odd numbers in each sum.

10
00:00:30,836 --> 00:00:34,422
Three of them give three times three. Call that count n.

11
00:00:34,522 --> 00:00:37,119
For one plus three plus five, n is three.

12
00:00:37,219 --> 00:00:40,831
So it seems that the first n odd numbers add up to n times n.

13
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:43,513
But why should odd numbers make squares at all?

14
00:00:43,613 --> 00:00:47,584
Five examples show a pattern. They do not prove it for every n.

15
00:00:47,684 --> 00:00:51,411
The question mark means: not proved yet. We need a reason.

16
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,370
A square number is a square of tiles.

17
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:57,663
Nine tiles make three rows of three:

18
00:00:57,763 --> 00:01:00,328
a three by three square, with side three.

19
00:01:00,428 --> 00:01:03,146
Each sum adds one more odd number. So ask:

20
00:01:03,246 --> 00:01:06,446
what does one more odd number add to a square of tiles?

21
00:01:06,546 --> 00:01:08,684
Start with the first odd number, one:

22
00:01:08,784 --> 00:01:10,628
one tile, a square with side one.

23
00:01:10,716 --> 00:01:14,118
Add the next odd number, three. Three tiles go around it:

24
00:01:14,218 --> 00:01:18,319
to the left, below, and in the corner. Together they make an L shape:

25
00:01:18,419 --> 00:01:22,683
a column and a row that share a corner. The square now has side two.

26
00:01:22,783 --> 00:01:26,745
One plus three is four tiles, the same four as in the sums.

27
00:01:26,845 --> 00:01:30,381
Each L has the color of its odd number, and its number lights up in

28
00:01:30,481 --> 00:01:30,862
the sums.

29
00:01:30,961 --> 00:01:34,275
The next L has five tiles, and makes side three.

30
00:01:34,375 --> 00:01:38,559
Seven tiles make side four. Nine tiles make side five.

31
00:01:38,659 --> 00:01:43,014
Each L adds one to the side. So after n Ls, the side is n.

32
00:01:43,114 --> 00:01:47,749
Here n counts the Ls, and each L is one odd number, so it is the same

33
00:01:47,849 --> 00:01:48,560
n as before.

34
00:01:49,844 --> 00:01:52,014
Why is each L the next odd number?

35
00:01:52,114 --> 00:01:54,711
Look at the L around the four by four square.

36
00:01:54,811 --> 00:01:58,800
It has a row of four, a column of four, and one corner.

37
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:00,741
Four plus four plus one is nine.

38
00:02:02,028 --> 00:02:06,408
The next L goes around the five by five square, and makes six by six.

39
00:02:06,508 --> 00:02:09,617
It is drawn faint, because we have not added it yet.

40
00:02:09,717 --> 00:02:12,634
It has five plus five plus one: eleven.

41
00:02:12,734 --> 00:02:15,219
Each L is two bigger than the one before:

42
00:02:15,319 --> 00:02:18,296
one more in its row, and one more in its column.

43
00:02:18,396 --> 00:02:22,848
The first L is the first tile: no row, no column, only its corner.

44
00:02:22,948 --> 00:02:27,224
It is one. So the Ls are one, three, five, seven, and so on:

45
00:02:27,324 --> 00:02:28,852
the odd numbers, in order.

46
00:02:30,644 --> 00:02:34,542
So adding the odd numbers in order is adding the Ls in order.

47
00:02:34,642 --> 00:02:37,090
After n Ls, the square has side n.

48
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:40,362
So the first n odd numbers add up to n times n.

49
00:02:40,462 --> 00:02:42,206
The question mark can go.

50
00:02:42,306 --> 00:02:45,798
We write n times n as n squared, n with a small two.

51
00:02:45,898 --> 00:02:49,036
The brace marks the n odd numbers, and the dots mean:

52
00:02:49,136 --> 00:02:50,236
and so on, in order.

53
00:02:51,828 --> 00:02:55,619
Pause here and predict. What is the sum of the first ten odd numbers?

54
00:02:58,711 --> 00:03:02,332
Ten Ls make a square with side ten: one hundred tiles.

55
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:06,512
The five new Ls are eleven, thirteen, fifteen, seventeen, and

56
00:03:06,612 --> 00:03:08,804
nineteen, each in its own color.

57
00:03:08,904 --> 00:03:13,068
The first L is one, and each of the nine Ls after it adds two:

58
00:03:13,168 --> 00:03:15,640
one plus nine times two is nineteen.

59
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:18,434
So the first ten odd numbers add up to one hundred.

60
00:03:19,728 --> 00:03:22,814
The first tile matters. Start at three instead:

61
00:03:22,914 --> 00:03:24,445
three plus five is eight.

62
00:03:24,545 --> 00:03:27,568
Without the first tile, the Ls go around a hole.

63
00:03:27,668 --> 00:03:30,534
Nine minus one is eight, and eight is not a square.

64
00:03:32,428 --> 00:03:33,638
One more thing.

65
00:03:33,738 --> 00:03:37,017
A sum of the first ten odd numbers stopped at nineteen.

66
00:03:37,117 --> 00:03:39,372
Where does a sum of n odd numbers stop?

67
00:03:39,472 --> 00:03:41,557
The L that makes side n tells us.

68
00:03:41,657 --> 00:03:44,382
It goes around a square of side n minus one.

69
00:03:44,482 --> 00:03:47,292
Here n is five, and n minus one is four.

70
00:03:47,392 --> 00:03:51,460
So it has n minus one, plus n minus one, plus one tiles.

71
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,264
The brackets keep each n minus one together.

72
00:03:54,364 --> 00:03:57,750
Two copies of n make two n, which means two times n.

73
00:03:57,850 --> 00:04:02,555
Take away the two ones, and add the corner: two n minus one. Check:

74
00:04:02,655 --> 00:04:04,410
n equals five gives nine.

75
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:07,640
N equals ten gives nineteen, where the sum stopped.

76
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:10,030
N equals one gives one, the first tile.

77
00:04:11,328 --> 00:04:15,576
So, the answer: the first n odd numbers add up to n squared.

78
00:04:15,676 --> 00:04:18,648
Every odd number is an L, and the Ls build squares.
